course: dictionary
lesson: 3867
title: Fruit words in French
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Framboise is a French word, not an English one. You may see it on cakes, jams and ice creams, and on menus and labels in English shops too. It is a noun, a word for a thing, and in French it comes with «une» in front, which means «a».
explain: The sentence «une fraise is a strawberry, une framboise is a raspberry and une myrtille is a blueberry» shows three fruit words side by side. Each one has «une» in front, and the English word comes after «is a». Fraise, framboise and myrtille all name fruit, so framboise must name a fruit too.
explain: The sentence is a context clue. It sits right next to the English word «raspberry», so you can work out what framboise means. Test it: swap «raspberry» in for framboise. The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: «Framboise» means «raspberry» in French.
fact: It is pronounced «from-BWAHZ».
fact: «Une» means «a» in French, so «une framboise» means «a raspberry».
fact: In English, framboise is often used on menus and labels for raspberry flavour, and it can also mean a raspberry liqueur, an alcoholic drink for adults.
fact: Other French fruit words include «fraise» (strawberry) and «pomme» (apple).
exercise: In the sentence «une framboise is a raspberry», what does framboise mean? | Blueberry | Apple | *Raspberry | Strawberry
exercise: Which French word in the sentence «une fraise is a strawberry, une framboise is a raspberry and une myrtille is a blueberry» means blueberry? | *Myrtille | Framboise | Fraise
exercise: You see «framboise» on a cake label in an English shop. What flavour is the cake most likely to be? | Mint | Banana | Chocolate | *Raspberry
test: Framboise is a French word. What does it mean in English? | *Raspberry | Blueberry | Cherry | Strawberry
test: Which French word means «strawberry»? | Myrtille | Pomme | Framboise | *Fraise
exam: Jayden sees «framboise» on a menu and asks what it is. Which answer is best? | It means a blue fruit, like a blueberry | It is an English word for a kind of bread | It means strawberry, as in fraise | *It is French for raspberry, so the flavour is probably raspberry
